WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.560
I could hear your voice...

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.550
Grim Reaper!

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.060
Critical trigger!

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.590
I give all the effects to Blaster Dark!

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.280
Oh, no...

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.240
Shadow Paladin...

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.370
I must have been waiting to meet this deck.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.720
I won't lose to anyone now...

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:33.730
I'm stronger than anyone now!

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.410
What lousy weather, huh?

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:21.110
Even though the national 
tournament is tomorrow...

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:24.570
The weather report said it's 
going to be a fine day tomorrow.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.160
Oh?

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.060
Aichi's not coming down...

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.480
Maybe I'll go get him.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.830
Aichi is concentrating on checking his deck.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.870
I think we should leave him be.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.350
I suppose you're right.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.810
Aichi...

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:02.600
This deck made me stronger.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.230
But I still have a ways to go.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.980
If I get even stronger,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:12.900
you won't say it isn't worth 
fighting me, will you, Kai?

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:19.340
Unexpected Visitor

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.570
Bye bye, Manager!

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:23.560
Be careful going home!

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.370
Good luck at nationals, Q4!

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.270
Leave it to us!

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.720
Aichi didn't come today either, huh?

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.360
Don't tell me taking off 
until nationals means he...

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:42.860
No, Brother wouldn't do that.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:47.370
I bet he's in his room right now, 
quivering under the pressure.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.360
"I'm scared! I'm scared!

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.450
Morikawa, help me!"

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:53.610
Kidding! Only kidding!

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.080
That'd never happen!

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:10.050
Sorry, we're already closed for the day...

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:17.540
You're...

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:20.380
...Ultra-rare's...

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.740
...K-Kourin!

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.760
What are you doing at Card Capital?!

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:28.680
It's obvious! She's here to visit me!

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.400
This is, like, whatchamacallit...

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.910
A modern-day Cinderella!

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.170
What are you, a princess?

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.100
Is Toshiki Kai here?

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:39.400
No, he's not around...

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:41.830
I have business with him. Bring him here.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:43.120
Easy for you to say...

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.840
I don't know where he is right now...

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.590
I'm in a hurry.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.480
Okay.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:51.960
You know where he is?

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:52.580
Yeah, well...

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:56.350
I didn't say anything because 
I was sure he'd get mad,

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.360
but this seems kind of important, so...

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.660
Please take me there.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.500
Here we go.  Hold on tight!

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:08.570
Uh... right!

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:11.710
Why, you...! Get your hands off of her!

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:12.570
Morikawa!

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:16.250
What do you want me to do?
There are traffic laws!

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:20.810
Wait!

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:22.910
Kourin!!

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.260
T-Turn over there...

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:30.250
Down that alley...

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:32.700
But slow down!

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:38.710
Wow, that was some ride...

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:40.030
He's here?

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:40.820
Yeah.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:43.090
See, he's playing right now.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.050
I lost!

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:47.290
Next.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:48.340
You go!

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:49.760
N-No way!

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:50.750
<i>You</i> go!

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.250
C-Cut it out!

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.000
That's enough.

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:57.750
Try to imagine how we feel when a guy 
like you takes out his anger on us.

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:59.250
Hey, Kai!

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:02.320
Hi! Good to see ya.

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.000
Been a while...

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:08.730
I don't know what you're so irritated about, 
but I think you oughta stop right about here.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:10.170
This is a bad habit.

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:11.870
It's none of your business.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:15.720
Hey, it's Ultra-rare!

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.390
What's she doing here?

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:18.830
She looks kinda scary...

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:21.270
Totally different from when she's singing!

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:23.560
Fight me!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:31.220
I'm going to test you, to see whether
it's worth talking to you or not.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:34.790
Fine.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.700
Huh?

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.650
Why do <i>I</i> have to be chained?

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:42.880
It's cool. You're in
 the best spot to watch the fight.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.650
Yeah, but if possible...

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.710
Don't be shy. You had fun last time, right?

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.310
I'm envious!

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:50.270
Lucky!

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:51.220
Yeah, really!

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:52.820
Oh, shut up!

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:55.180
Are you ready?

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:57.990
Yes. I know this system.

00:06:58.430 --> 00:06:59.680
Ready when you are.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:05.350
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:05.350
Stand up the Vanguard!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.580
Amber Dragon, Dawn!

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:19.210
Brugal!

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.510
I go first, and I draw!

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:25.780
I ride Lake Maiden, Lien!

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:34.480
Brugal moves, and I activate Lien's skill!

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.310
I drop one card from my hand

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:38.860
and draw one card.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.240
She traded in

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:43.310
a card with 10000 shield?

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:44.680
I draw.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:48.690
I ride Amber Dragon, Daylight.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:53.550
I activate Dawn's skill.

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:56.530
When I ride Daylight on this unit,

00:07:56.530 --> 00:08:00.770
I can take one Amber Dragon, Dusk 
from my deck and add it to my hand.

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:03.230
And then, with Daylight's skill,

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:07.100
while Dawn is in the Soul,
 Daylight receives +2000 power.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:11.210
I attack Lake Maiden, Lien!

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:13.510
I-It's coming?!

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:20.400
Drive trigger check.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:28.220
I stand and draw.

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:31.230
As always, this is bad for my heart!

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:32.650
It's fun once you get used to it.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:34.250
I don't wanna get used to it!

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:36.160
I ride Beast Knight, Garmall!

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:44.620
With Garmall's skill, I 
drop one card from my hand

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:47.330
and call Snogal from my deck!

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:53.020
I move Brugal

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:55.090
and call one more Snogal.

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:57.770
When there's more than 
one Snogal on the field,

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.790
each gains +1000 power 
for every other Snogal.

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:04.090
With a boost from Snogal,

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:05.180
Garmall attacks!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.570
Drive trigger check.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:15.070
Critical trigger.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:17.820
I add +5000 to the power of Brugal.

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:20.580
And I give the extra critical to Garmall!

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:26.830
With a boost from Snogal,

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:28.670
Brugal attacks!

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:34.230
I guard with Gattling Claw Dragon.

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:35.000
Which means...

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:38.550
I was right!

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:47.310
I see.

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:51.280
She sacrificed a 10000 
shield unit in preparation

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.530
and she has three kinds of 
criticals to choose from.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:57.270
On top of that, she has the Snogals, which 
get stronger just by being out there together.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:00.620
So she's totally focusing on attacking...

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.410
I stand and draw.

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:06.690
I ride Amber Dragon, Dusk!

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:13.660
While Daylight is in the Soul,

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.010
Dusk gains +1000 power!

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:18.250
I call Lava Arm Dragon and Daylight!

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:23.320
I activate Daylight's skill.

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:26.300
When this unit is called to the rear-guard,

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.740
if I drop one grade 3 Kagero,

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:32.980
I can take one Amber Dragon, Eclipse 
from my deck and add it to my hand.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.880
What's he doin'?

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:37.540
Isn't that like trading one 
card for the same card?

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:40.570
Grade 3 are really strong cards,

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:43.380
but if you draw too many, you 
won't know what to do with them,

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:45.490
unlike a grade 2 with the 
ability to intercept.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:46.510
I get it!

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:51.690
So if he has one in his hand, it's better 
if there aren't as many in his deck, right?

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:54.100
With a boost from Daylight,

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:55.670
Dusk attacks!

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:02.500
Drive trigger check.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:07.770
When Dusk attacks the opponent's Vanguard,

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:10.520
it gains +2000 power.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:13.800
Hot! Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:15.470
Damage check.

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:18.690
Knock it off! You did that 
on purpose, didn't you?!

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:22.560
I attack with Lava Arm Dragon!

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:25.940
When this unit attacks, it gains +2000 power!

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:39.690
That's the end of my turn.

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:43.250
Yeesh, that guy Kai... did he 
pick a fight with that idol?

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:49.410
That girl, Kourin, is it...?
I have no idea why she came here.

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:52.680
It looks to me like this is the first 
meeting between her and Kai, but...

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:58.020
Come to think of it, Aichi's 
met her a number of times...

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:05.240
I'm a bit surprised that you're a 
fighter with a delicate playing style.

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:08.490
If there's something you 
wanna say, just say it.

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:14.500
You're the one who had Aichi Sendou 
look for that power, aren't you?

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:33.680
You're the one who had Aichi Sendou 
look for that power, aren't you?

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:36.830
It's about Aichi? I see...

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.070
You "see"?

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:39.520
He chose it.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:41.990
H-Hey...

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:44.240
And who made him do it?!

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.620
It's my turn, and I draw!

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:49.100
I ride Fang of Light, Garmall!

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:53.950
I drop Marron from my hand.

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:55.740
Then I call Snogal from my deck!

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:03.120
On top of that, Fang of Light, Garmall

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:06.650
gains +1000 power for each Snogal and Brugal!

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:10.220
Four of them, so that's +4000...

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:12.970
I call High Dog Breeder, Akane!

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:17.440
Akane's Counterblast!

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:20.370
I call Snogal from the deck.

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:25.740
Brugal exits the field.

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:29.700
Four Snogals, each with 9000 power...

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:31.880
A perfect formation...

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:33.900
This is what I call a "Blizzard Formation".

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:37.820
With a boost from Snogal,

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:40.480
Fang of Light, Garmall attacks!

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:46.420
First check...

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:48.090
Critical trigger!

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.350
I give the extra critical to Garmall

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:52.210
and the power to Snogal!

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:55.350
Second check...

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:01.820
Draw trigger.

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:04.660
I add +5000 to the power of Dusk.

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:07.050
And then I draw.

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:09.110
With a boost from Snogal,

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.800
High Dog Breeder, Akane attacks!

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:16.560
I guard with Embodiment of Armor, Bahr.

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:27.590
Snogal, full power!

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:30.340
I guard with Dragon Monk, Genjo!

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:32.600
Genjo?!

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:43.830
<i>This</i> is definitely not that power.

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:51.990
Why did Aichi Sendou have to get that power?!

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:55.900
I don't really know...

00:14:56.230 --> 00:15:00.970
If you use this, you'll 
expand your power even more.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:05.640
Now, take this deck.

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:10.290
Take it, and it will give you strength.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:17.020
Why did you have him seek out that 
power when you can't even stop him?!

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:24.410
I stand and draw.

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:28.480
I ride Amber Dragon, Eclipse!

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:36.900
While Dusk is in the Soul, 
Eclipse gains +1000 power.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:41.670
I call Demonic Dragon Mage, Kimnara

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:44.740
and Dragonic Overlord!

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:51.970
How do you know Kai's name?

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:56.050
It was my dream to be able to 
fight with you like this, Kai.

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:58.960
I'm gonna get stronger!

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:00.840
I swear I'm gonna get stronger!

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:10.970
It's like the cards are 
lending me their power...

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:16.340
Is this what you were talking about 
when you told me to "picture it", Kai?

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:19.900
Aichi... I can't fight you...

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:25.290
Answer me!

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:31.550
Yeah. It's my fault.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:38.640
I've seen that power before.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.760
I couldn't stop him, either.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:49.020
No. I didn't even know

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:51.020
<i>how</i> to stop him.

00:16:53.980 --> 00:16:57.280
But it might have been a simple thing.

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:00.740
Kimnara's Counterblast!

00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:05.230
I can retire one of my opponent's 
grade 1 rear-guard units!

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:07.240
I select Snogal!

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:10.690
Eclipse's Counterblast!

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:15.760
When Eclipse's attack hits, I can retire 
two of my opponent's rear-guard units.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.600
I attack with a boost from Daylight!

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:23.680
I won't let that happen!

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.550
I guard with Alabaster Owl!

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:28.980
And then High Dog Breeder, Akane intercepts!

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:34.180
First check.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:35.870
Draw trigger.

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:39.050
I add +5000 to the power of Eclipse.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:42.040
It'll be for nothing if there's 
no trigger on the next check.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:46.240
Second check.

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:47.970
Critical trigger.

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:50.200
That's another +5000 power.

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:52.280
I give you 2 damage.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:04.410
Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:07.910
I activate Eclipse's skill!

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:09.480
I retire two of your units!

00:18:15.890 --> 00:18:18.310
Her "Blizzard Formation"...

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:20.450
Now she can't power up!

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:24.560
He blew away a lineup like 
that in just one turn!

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:25.700
He's got the strength of an ogre...

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:28.410
I attack with Dragonic Overlord!

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.010
I guard with Epona!

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:32.000
Lava Arm Dragon!

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:33.920
My other Epona!

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:36.010
That's the end of my turn.

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:38.420
You said "a simple thing"...?

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:44.890
I could exceed that power.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.500
That's all.

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.570
I stand and draw.

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:56.030
Do you seriously intend 
to surpass that power?

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:56.790
Yeah.

00:18:56.790 --> 00:18:59.030
Can you stop Aichi Sendou?

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:01.990
I will stop him.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:10.540
I call Knight of Conviction, Bors 
and Knight of Silence, Gallatin!

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:12.600
Snogal moves.

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:15.980
I attack with Garmall!

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.690
I guard with Wyvern Guard, Barri.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:23.750
Twin drive, first check!

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:25.910
Second check...

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:28.290
Critical trigger!

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:32.280
I attack with Gallatin, who gets all 
the effects, plus a boost from Snogal!

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:37.570
I guard with Tahr and Nehalem!

00:19:42.350 --> 00:19:45.770
Yeesh... What a meathead...

00:19:47.090 --> 00:19:50.780
If he's worred about Aichi, he should 
just come right out and say so.

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:54.400
I attack with Overlord!

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:01.850
No guard.

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:53.400
Aichi...

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:57.690
Are you nervous, Kamui?

00:20:58.440 --> 00:20:59.980
Oh... no...

00:21:00.630 --> 00:21:04.490
Brother doesn't seem like his usual self...

00:21:04.710 --> 00:21:07.310
Don't worry. We're going to win.

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:10.740
After all, I have this deck...

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:12.700
B-Brother!

00:21:13.140 --> 00:21:15.150
What is that deck?!

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:17.170
Where's your Blaster Blade?

00:21:18.390 --> 00:21:19.630
I don't know.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.340
Brother!

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:27.290
This deck is gonna make me even stronger!

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:29.970
And then, I'm sure... Kai...

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:48.820
I couldn't stop him...

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:53.250
Aichi...

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:58.540
What is that power?

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:01.420
Psyqualia.

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:04.000
Psyqualia?

00:22:12.200 --> 00:22:13.490
Stand up,

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:15.110
Vanguard!

00:23:51.180 --> 00:23:53.160
That deck Aichi has...

00:23:53.160 --> 00:23:54.330
Blaster Dark!

00:23:54.330 --> 00:23:58.620
Right. AL4's Ren Suzugamori was using 
it at the last national tournament.

00:23:58.620 --> 00:23:59.500
I was right...

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:01.620
I wonder what's wrong with Brother...

00:24:01.620 --> 00:24:03.900
And where did he get that deck?

00:24:03.900 --> 00:24:05.130
The national tournament...

00:24:05.130 --> 00:24:07.180
I'm sad that Kai's not here...

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:10.420
...but I'm sure he'll come back after I win.

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:12.590
Next time: Shadow Paladin.

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:14.570
I have this deck.

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:18.370
I can't get even the slightest 
picture of myself losing.
